  "note": "Machine-readable snapshot of the curated public API. Generated from the installed package; tests/packaging/test_public_api.py asserts equality including dataclass field ORDER and the exact value of every string constant. This is the SHARED, PLATFORM-WIDE Ugence Policy Authority (ADR docs/architecture/ADR_UGENCE_POLICY_AUTHORITY.md, P-1/P-10) \u2014 internal platform infrastructure, not a customer-facing module and not a UVI engine. UVI is its FIRST policy-family adapter (P-2), registered behind the PolicyFamilyAdapter protocol; the generic core imports and branches on no policy family. Organizational approval remains EXTERNAL (P-5): the authority verifies externally produced approval evidence through an injected boundary owned by the composition root, and the only shipped verifier is DenyAllApprovalVerifier. v0.1 REJECTS issuance of any artifact carrying a non-empty unstructured supersedes_ref (emptiness is supersedes_ref.strip()) with the stable reason SUPERSESSION_REFERENCE_UNSUPPORTED; there is no permissive supersession posture and structured successor references are deferred (P-6/P-7). Revocation is mandatory-signed, entitlement-authorized, and re-verified during resolution (P-8). Trust anchors are defensively copied and exposed read-only. The in-memory registry is reference-grade and PROCESS-LOCAL only. Constructing any public dataclass is NOT authenticity \u2014 only resolve_policy produces an authority-evaluated resolution.",
